# File: scripts/__tests__/sdlc-execute.test.mjs, scripts/__tests__/plugin-commands.test.mjs, scripts/__tests__/steering-contract.test.mjs, hooks/register.test.ts
# Generated from: specs/464-run-each-sdlc-step-on-its-assigned-claude-code-model/requirements.md
Feature: Run each nmg-sdlc step on its assigned Claude Code model
  Every nmg-sdlc step runs on the Claude Code model suited to its workload,
  and the user's session model is never changed.

  @SCN001
  Scenario: fresh stage workers start on their stage model
    Given an issue with no recorded repairable failure in the current invocation
    When /sdlc-execute dispatches start, implement, verify, and deliver workers
    Then the herdr agent start arguments after "--" end with "--model haiku", "--model haiku", "--model opus", and "--model haiku" respectively
    And they begin with "--plugin-dir <plugin-root> --permission-mode <mode>"

  @SCN002
  Scenario: repair re-dispatch escalates to opus
    Given the controller recorded a failure with reason code "verification_not_green" for the issue
    When it dispatches the next implement worker
    Then the worker arguments end with "--model opus"
    And a recorded "pr_evidence_pending" or "mergeability_reverification_required" failure keeps the stage model
    And after a stage passes the next dispatch uses its stage model again

  @SCN003
  Scenario: automated command files declare their model
    Given the generated commands/sdlc-status.md, commands/sdlc-verify-code.md, and commands/sdlc-open-pr.md
    Then their frontmatter model is "haiku", "opus", and "haiku" respectively
    And each file equals renderAutomatedCommandMarkdown output

  @SCN004
  Scenario: hooks-registered commands run on their model without changing the session model
    Given an interactive session on model "claude-sonnet-5-5"
    When the user runs "/sdlc-write-spec #7" and the workflow turn, a Continue turn, and the Finished nudge are submitted by the hooks module
    Then every main-loop turn.step request names model "opus" with its effort unchanged
    And a subagent turn.step request keeps its own model
    And when the user runs "/sdlc-execute #7" its main-loop requests name model "haiku"
    And $.session.model() still reports "claude-sonnet-5-5"

  @SCN005
  Scenario: the override ends when the user moves on or picks a model
    Given "/sdlc-draft-issue" set an "opus" override in a session on model "claude-sonnet-5-5"
    When the user submits a composer prompt, or the session model changes to "claude-haiku-5-5"
    Then later main-loop turn.step requests keep the session's own model
    And a headless refusal or render failure of an interactive command sets no override

  @SCN006
  Scenario: agents and steering declare the stage models
    Given the packaged agents and the steering Agent Files table
    Then starter is "haiku", spec-implementer is "haiku", architecture-reviewer is "opus", and deliverer is "haiku"
    And each equals SDLC_MODELS.stages for its step
    And SDLC_MODELS.commands has one entry for every interactive and automated command

  @SCN007
  Scenario: a model-routed worker start failure stops dispatch
    Given herdr agent start exits non-zero for a launch with "--model haiku"
    When the controller dispatches the implement stage
    Then /sdlc-execute stops with "agent_start_failed"
    And no prompt is sent to that worker
    And the owned pane is closed unless --retain-worker was passed
